%% Invalid-guard fixture.  fail is defined nowhere, as a guard or in a body:
%% it is no guard predicate of the catalogue (GLP-Spec appendix-guards.tex) and
%% no unit clause defines it, so in guard position it is an unknown guard and
%% the clause is refused at compile time.  The procedure is declared, so it is
%% the guard that is refused and not the clause of an undeclared procedure
%% (TGLP Definition "Typed GLP Program").
procedure bad_guard(_).
bad_guard(X?) :- fail | X = done.
